For what it's worth I think the proper way to go forward here is some sort of custom `IBindableNumber` implementation just for this, that essentially does something like the following:

```csharp
public OptionalBindableNumber<T> : IBindableNumber<T>
{
	private bool valueWasChanged;

	public OptionalBindableNumber(T initialValue = default)
	{
		ValueChanged += _ => valueWasChanged = true;
	}

	public T Value
	{
		get => valueWasChanged ? base.Value : base.Default;
		set => base.Value = value;
	}

	public bool IsDefault => !valueWasChanged;

	public void SetDefault => valueWasChanged = false;

	// and probably more things as required, incl. (de)serialisation
}
```

but this will 100% require larger amendments both game- and framework-side (because `SetDefault` is not virtual, and game is hard-coupled to `BindableNumber` to create settings controls, etc.).
